"""Overcooked V2 demo_cook_simple policy.

Map layout: two disjoint rooms connected only through a shared pot cell.
agent_0's room contains the always-on recipe indicator and all three
ingredient supplies; agent_1's room contains ingredient supplies 0 and 1,
the plate pile and the delivery station, but never sees the recipe
indicator (it is outside agent_1's reachable view, and there is no button
indicator in this layout either). Recipes only ever use ingredient 0 or
ingredient 1 (never 2), so this information asymmetry cleanly assigns
roles: agent_0 senses the recipe and feeds the pot, agent_1 plates,
collects and delivers whatever the pot produces.

There is no in-observation global position, so each seat localizes itself
every step by matching the observed static-object channels (walls, pot,
recipe indicator, plate pile, ingredient piles) against the fixed, known
map: all 24 reachable floor cells give a unique 5x5 static crop, so exact
match localization is unambiguous. Navigation uses precomputed
breadth-first shortest-path "next action" tables per named destination,
computed offline (not at import time) and embedded here as literal data,
since module-scope calls, while loops and numpy/collections imports are
not permitted in this file.
"""

